in a future release of nethack perhaps food could be handled along these lines:

1) during eating it takes one turn to consume 100 points of nutrition. a food
    ration would take 8 turns to eat, if not interrupted, a K-ration 4 turns,
    and so on.

2) if you're interrupted while eating then you get fed according to what you
    consumed, i.e. if you're stopped after the 5th turn while eating a food
    ration you are given 500 nutrition points.

3) for non-perishable foods (non-corpse) if you continue to eat in 1 or 2 moves
    then you may finish the rest of that meal (the leftover concept). if you
    don't continue eating within 1 or 2 moves the food item disappears.

4) for perishable (corpse) foods, you run the risk of the food becoming
    tainted if you don't continue eating before the salmonella time-out.

5) when magic is awarded for consuming appropriate foods should be a random
    number within the number of turns it takes to eat the food. the magic
    reward may sometimes not occur if you don't finish your meal.

over-eating seems to be appropriately handled.

